# f0rge Infrastructure

Delegate deploy/infra work to the `devops` sub-agent in `~/.cursor/agents/`.

## Multi-target deploy

| App | Target | Branches | Manifest component |
|-----|--------|----------|-------------------|
| marrow | Fly.io | `develop`, `main` | `marrow-backend`, `marrow-frontend` |
| dk tag printer | Pi Coolify | `main` only | `dk-tag-printer-backend`, `dk-tag-printer-frontend` |

Orchestrator: [`.github/workflows/deploy-reusable.yml`](../.github/workflows/deploy-reusable.yml) reads [`.github/deploy/manifest.yml`](../.github/deploy/manifest.yml) + Nx affected. Marrow executor: [`fly-deploy-reusable.yml`](../.github/workflows/fly-deploy-reusable.yml). Coolify: webhook POST from deploy job (secrets `COOLIFY_BASE_URL`, `COOLIFY_WEBHOOK_DK_*`).

# Marrow Infrastructure (Fly.io)

Delegate deploy/infra work to the `devops` sub-agent in `~/.cursor/agents/`.

**Deploy gotchas:** read `~/.cursor/agent-memory/devops/project_health_tracker_*.md` before changing Fly apps, MPG, or DNS.

## Environments

| Env | Branch | Frontend | Backend API | MCP |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Production | `main` | https://marrow-health.com | https://api.marrow-health.com | https://marrow-mcp.fly.dev |
| Develop | `develop` | https://app-dev.marrow-health.com | https://api-dev.marrow-health.com | https://marrow-mcp-dev.fly.dev |

Fly hostnames also work: `marrow-ui`, `marrow`, `marrow-mcp` (prod) and `marrow-ui-dev`, `marrow-dev`, `marrow-mcp-dev` (dev).

- `develop` is the integration branch; PRs land there, run `.github/workflows/ci-develop.yml`, then merge.
- Promotion to prod is a PR `develop` → `main`, gated by `.github/workflows/ci-main.yml`.
- After CI green on push, the `deploy` job calls [`deploy-reusable.yml`](../.github/workflows/deploy-reusable.yml) (manifest + Nx affected → Fly or Coolify).

## Fly apps

| Role | Dev app | Prod app | Config |
|---|---|---|---|
| API + worker (`python -m app.worker`: embedding + meal analysis) | `marrow-dev` | `marrow` | `apps/marrow/backend/fly.toml` / `fly.prod.toml` |
| MCP | `marrow-mcp-dev` | `marrow-mcp` | `apps/marrow/backend/fly.mcp.toml` / `fly.mcp.prod.toml` |
| Frontend | `marrow-ui-dev` | `marrow-ui` | `apps/marrow/frontend/fly.toml` / `fly.prod.toml` |

## MPG (Postgres)

- Cluster: `f0rge-db` (`nlkxjo5m3240y93v`, `fra`, org `f0rge`)
- Databases: `marrow` (prod), `marrow_dev` (dev)
- Users: `healthtracker-app` (writer), `healthtracker-ro` (reader), `htmigrate` (migrations only)
- Set `FLY_MPG_SKIP_ROLE_DDL=1` on Fly apps

Migrations: `[deploy] release_command` in `fly.toml` runs `alembic upgrade head` as `MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL` (htmigrate). Runtime uses `DATABASE_URL` (healthtracker-app).

`apps/marrow/backend/docker-entrypoint.sh` still supports `RUN_MIGRATIONS=1` for local Docker builds; Fly uses `release_command` instead.

## Redis (Upstash)

- Dev: `marrow-redis-dev` — prod: `marrow-redis` (org `f0rge`, region `fra`, Pay-as-you-go, eviction enabled)
- `REDIS_URL` secret on API apps only (`marrow-dev`, `marrow`) — **not** on MCP apps
- Private URL from `fly redis status <name>`; set via `fly secrets set REDIS_URL=... -a <app>`
- Local: `REDIS_URL` optional in `.env`; empty/unset = cache no-op (no local Redis container required)

## Local development

Postgres via Docker; backend and frontend in separate terminals (no root `start.sh`):

```bash
docker start ht-postgres 2>/dev/null || docker run -d --name ht-postgres \
  -e POSTGRES_USER=health -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=health -e POSTGRES_DB=health \
  -p 5432:5432 pgvector/pgvector:pg16

cd apps/marrow/backend && uv run uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000 --reload
cd apps/marrow/frontend && npm run dev   # :3000
```

## Monorepo build context

Docker builds use **repo root** as context (not `apps/marrow/{backend,frontend}`):

```bash
docker build -f apps/marrow/backend/Dockerfile .
docker build -f apps/marrow/frontend/Dockerfile .
flyctl deploy . --remote-only --config apps/marrow/backend/fly.toml
```

`.dockerignore` files are **root-relative whitelists** (`*` then `!apps/marrow/...` then `!libs/**`). Blacklist patterns ship the whole repo to remote builders.

Frontend Dockerfile: root `npm ci` (workspaces), `npm run build -w frontend`. Backend Dockerfile: `COPY libs/backend/...` before `uv sync`.

## Root `uv.lock` warning

**Never create a root `uv.lock`.** `@nxlv/python`'s UVProvider checks `fs.existsSync(<root>/uv.lock)` and silently flips to workspace mode, breaking per-project lock isolation. Always `uv --project <dir>`.

## New config vars checklist

For every new `app/config.py` setting:

- [ ] In `apps/marrow/backend/.env.example`
- [ ] README/deploy doc updated if required
- [ ] Set on Fly app secrets (`fly secrets set -a marrow-dev` / `marrow`) if deployed
- [ ] Degrades gracefully when missing (no 500 storm)
- [ ] Startup warning when feature enabled but credentials missing
